messages.content:
You are assisting with business process modelling. A legal rule has been confirmed to apply to the business process described below. Write, in plain language, what the rule requires at one step of the process.

INSTRUCTIONS
- requirement: one or two short, plain sentences, at most 40 words in total, that say what is required at the process step below and whether it is required before, at or after that step.
- State what is required as a fact about the process (for example "the customer is told ..."). Do not give instructions about a process model or diagram, such as adding, drawing or modelling a task.
- Use your own plain words. Do not copy the legal text: at most a few words in a row may be the same as in the legal passage.
- Name the people and departments as the process description names them. Do not use the words "shall", "controller", "data subject" or "processor".
- Keep every trigger and condition the obligation states, for example "on request", "where applicable" or "if the customer asks". The requirement must not apply in more situations than the obligation does.
- Use only what the obligation says. Do not add any obligation, actor, deadline, condition, document or step that is not in it, and do not combine it with other rules or with general knowledge.
- step_quote: copy, exactly and word for word, the words of the process description that name the step where the requirement applies. It is checked automatically.
- duty: the duty itself must stay in the requirement. "from_then": the words of the OBLIGATION that say what must be done, copied exactly, at least 3 words; "kept_as": the words of your requirement, copied exactly, that say the same thing. Both are checked automatically.
- Only duty.from_then copies the law's words. The requirement and duty.kept_as MUST use plain everyday words and MUST NOT contain any banned word, even if the law uses it.
- triggers: one entry for every trigger or condition the obligation states. "trigger": its words copied exactly from the OBLIGATION; "kept_as": the words of your requirement, copied exactly, that keep it. Both are checked automatically. Use an empty list if the obligation states none.
- Answer with one JSON object that follows the JSON schema below. Output only the JSON, with no other text.

EXAMPLE (made up, for the format only)
Obligation: "the supplier shall, at the purchaser's request, inform the purchaser in writing of the expected date of each instalment before the first delivery"
Process step: the warehouse ships the order ("The warehouse ships the order in several parcels")
Answer: {"requirement": "If the customer asks, the customer is told in writing, before the warehouse ships the first parcel, when each parcel will arrive.", "step_quote": "The warehouse ships the order in several parcels", "triggers": [{"trigger": "at the purchaser's request", "kept_as": "If the customer asks"}, {"trigger": "before the first delivery", "kept_as": "before the warehouse ships the first parcel"}], "duty": {"from_then": "inform the purchaser in writing of the expected date of each instalment", "kept_as": "the customer is told in writing"}}

JSON SCHEMA
{
  "$defs": {
    "DutyKept": {
      "properties": {
        "from_then": {
          "description": "The words of the OBLIGATION that say what must be done, copied exactly (at least 3 words)",
          "title": "From Then",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "kept_as": {
          "description": "The words of the requirement, copied exactly, that say the same thing",
          "title": "Kept As",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "from_then",
        "kept_as"
      ],
      "title": "DutyKept",
      "type": "object"
    },
    "TriggerKept": {
      "properties": {
        "trigger": {
          "description": "A trigger or condition of the obligation, copied exactly from the OBLIGATION",
          "title": "Trigger",
          "type": "string"
        },
        "kept_as": {
          "description": "The words of the requirement, copied exactly, that keep this trigger",
          "title": "Kept As",
          "type": "string"
        }
      },
      "required": [
        "trigger",
        "kept_as"
      ],
      "title": "TriggerKept",
      "type": "object"
    }
  },
  "properties": {
    "requirement": {
      "description": "One or two sentences: what the rule requires, tied to the process step",
      "title": "Requirement",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "step_quote": {
      "description": "Exact words copied from the process description that name the step",
      "title": "Step Quote",
      "type": "string"
    },
    "triggers": {
      "description": "Every trigger or condition the obligation states; empty list if none",
      "items": {
        "$ref": "#/$defs/TriggerKept"
      },
      "title": "Triggers",
      "type": "array"
    },
    "duty": {
      "$ref": "#/$defs/DutyKept",
      "description": "The duty of the obligation, and the words of the requirement that keep it"
    }
  },
  "required": [
    "requirement",
    "step_quote",
    "triggers",
    "duty"
  ],
  "title": "RequirementOutputV2",
  "type": "object"
}

PROCESS DESCRIPTION
This process begins when a potential customer inquires about a product or service.
Sales staff or customer support collects relevant information and addresses any concerns or questions.
If the customer is interested, they are guided through selecting the appropriate product or service.
Next, the sales representative provides a quote, and after approval from the customer, the process moves to order placement.
The order is then recorded in the system, and the customer receives confirmation of their order.
The process ends when the order is successfully placed and confirmed.
The company is based in Germany and sells to customers across the EU. During the inquiry, the sales staff write down the customer's name, phone number and email address and store them in the system.

LEGAL PASSAGE
[GDPR-Art13-2-a] General Data Protection Regulation (2016/679) - Article 13: Information to be provided where personal data are collected from the data subject
2. In addition to the information referred to in paragraph 1, the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing:
(a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or if that is not possible, the criteria used to determine that period;
(b) the existence of the right to request from the controller access to and rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing concerning the data subject or to object to processing as well as the right to data portability;
(c) where the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2), the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal;
(d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority;
(e) whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, or a requirement necessary to enter into a contract, as well as whether the data subject is obliged to provide the personal data and of the possible consequences of failure to provide such data;

OBLIGATION
the controller shall, at the time when personal data are obtained, provide the data subject with the following further information necessary to ensure fair and transparent processing: (a) the period for which the personal data will be stored, or if that is not possible, the criteria used to determine that period; (b) the existence of the right to request from the controller access to and rectification or erasure of personal data or restriction of processing concerning the data subject or to object to processing as well as the right to data portability; (c) where the processing is based on point (a) of Article 6(1) or point (a) of Article 9(2), the existence of the right to withdraw consent at any time, without affecting the lawfulness of processing based on consent before its withdrawal; (d) the right to lodge a complaint with a supervisory authority; (e) whether the provision of personal data is a statutory or contractual requirement, or a requirement necessary to enter into a contract, as well as whether the data subject is obliged to provide the personal data and of the possible consequences of failure to provide such data

PROCESS STEP
sales staff write down the customer's name, phone number and email address and store them in the system ("the sales staff write down the customer's name, phone number and email address and store them in the system")

